{"type":"match","data":{"path":{"text":"discover.hubpages.com/Endangered Birds Of Thailand.txt"},"lines":{"text":"Spoon-billed Sandpipers are in such rapid decline that the population estimate of 240-500 mature individuals is almost certainly very optimistic, some ornithologists suggest that there are fewer than 200 left. This species is unique amongst wader species in having a spatulate bill which it uses in a plucking and a sieving motion to find invertebrates in mudflats and salt pans.\n"},"line_number":38,"absolute_offset":2703,"submatches":[{"match":{"text":"mature individuals"},"start":90,"end":108}]}}
